    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0161" n="153" xml:id="pg153"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1391: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Representative of the President</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-02-06T14:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1939—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. With reference to my telegram No. 15 dated February 3, 6 p.m., Zúñiga
                    Montúfar and I discussed the advisability of having the note referred to therein
                    delivered in person by Ocheltree acting for the Permanent Secretariat. I am
                    inclined to favor this as he could informally explain the technical features of
                    the matter with a view to allaying Honduran objections to the aerial
                    reconnaissance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
